tablepro for Ubuntu
===================

This is the debian/ directory of the source package TablePro uploads to its
Launchpad PPA. It lives in the upstream tree under build-aux/debian.
build-aux/packaging/build-source.sh copies it to debian/ and writes
debian/changelog for the version and Ubuntu series being built.

Sources: tablepro_X.Y.Z.orig.tar.xz is the meson dist tarball.
tablepro_X.Y.Z.orig-vendor.tar.xz holds vendor/ from cargo vendor
--versioned-dirs, with the source replacement cargo printed as
vendor/cargo-config.toml. dpkg-source unpacks it into vendor/, and
debian/rules copies the replacement to .cargo/config.toml before it
configures, so the build needs no network.

Toolchain: the package build-depends on rustc-X.Y and cargo-X.Y, X.Y being
the workspace rust-version, and debian/rules puts /usr/lib/rust-X.Y/bin first
on PATH. build-aux/packaging/check_packaging.py keeps the three in step.
Ubuntu 26.04 gets them from ppa:rust-toolchain/staging, which the PPA depends
on; Ubuntu 26.10 has them in its archive.

Versions: X.Y.Z-0ppaN~YY.MM, as Launchpad's PPA guide describes for a
package built for several series. The revision 0 marks a package Debian does
not carry, so any archive version of X.Y.Z sorts above it. ppaN counts the
uploads of one upstream version. The series version keeps each series'
version unique and sorts a later series higher. It leaves out the word
ubuntu, which dpkg-source reads as an Ubuntu upload by a non-Ubuntu
maintainer, and a third dotted part, which lintian reads as a binary NMU.
An upstream pre-release such as 0.2.0-rc.1 becomes 0.2.0~rc.1, which sorts
below 0.2.0.

debian/copyright is generated from data/licenses/third-party.json by
build-aux/update-third-party-licenses.sh. Do not edit it by hand.
